# Opt98 + Opt99 (2026-10-31, config LN; both inert unless set): the split lockstep group's y push (STRATA_PF_SPLITF / SPLIT2) no longer drains the GPU.
# STRATA_PF_PUSH_NOSYNC=1: no cudaStreamSynchronize after the y push. On the tgcu shim every stream is one in-order queue (cudaStreamWaitEvent is a no-op,
# cudaStreamSynchronize / cudaEventSynchronize synchronize everything), so that call waited for the card to finish chunk i's front: ~25 ms of the 56 ms period
# per chunk-layer at 33K. The relaxed bulk push (TGCU_H2D_RELAX, >= PIPE_MIN) is synchronous on the host, so the link is idle when cudaMemcpyAsync returns and
# the next x download cannot overlap it. STRATA_PF_Y2=1: a second y landing buffer (mac_y_dev2, odd chunks of a group, its own combine event; +T*N*4 bytes in
# bytes_needed and carve). STRATA_PF_MAC_STATS adds `ywait` (the host-side wait for the buffer's last combine; not measured under NOSYNC).
# Measured (ABBA vs config LM, fresh restart per arm): 33K 967.5 -> 991.0 tok/s (+2.4 %), 8K 831.7 -> 834.8, 2.5K 282.2 -> 282.6; Y2 alone is neutral (968.1 vs 968.1).
